  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/98b3193783f0ac19bcb78035b133ad8dbf956528dfb7474606cc586d3bfecc34.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $90{\\text{\u00a0in}}^{2}.$   What is the area of $\u25b3BCD$ rounded to the nearest integer?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by finding the area of $\u25b3ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\u25b3ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16\\cdot 21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{56}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =168\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{56}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =139.278\u2026 \\\\  & \u2248139{\\text{\u00a0in}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of  $\u25b3ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $\u25b3BCD.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{\u25b3BCD} & ={A}_{\u25b3ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =139-90 \\\\  & =49{\\text{\u00a0in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
